#11021
book ethernaughts~
a book on ethernaughts~
This large book outlines the construction of ethernaughts.~
~
8 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
book account~
The Ethernaught and it's less glorious cousin the Battle-Ward are the result
ofa glorious union of gnomish technology and arcane magiks.  If not for the
magik of the ghoul magi and the elven elementalists, we would not have been
able to contain the amount of energy produced by the steam turbines nor could
we shield the pilots from these extreme temperatures. The Ethernaught
functions on a simple idea that's application is nigh impossible. The pilot
controls the more advanced movements, wielding of the arms and firing of the
flame cannons that are mounted. Yet, by providing a low grade consciousness,
that of an animal into the metal, these golem like creatures can react much as
a well trained war horse would. As proven by our battles with Zanzen, each
Ethernaught is capable of decimating enemy ranks as well as inspiring fear
into our enemies.  Their bulk and massive size makes them difficult to move
across great distances. It is best to keep them on defensive positions where
there is time to position them in the most beneficial areas.
~
#11022
history of Kinterownt~
a history of Kinterownt~
This large volume highlights the history of this city.~
~
8 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 0 0
E
history kinterownt~
0 K

  The founding of Kinterownt by the great gnomish warriors, Dilindi and
Kaliendi. The great cavern is found and work begins making it a great
city and fortress.


50K
  The first alliance among the dwarves to the northwest inside the
mine and fortress of Sorrow is established. The growing human prescense
at the feet of the mountain is ignored.

150 K
  The humans are victorious in defending their city against the barbarian
menace. Talks begin to import our iron and steel to the city.

175 K
  The humans reject our offer of trade. They wish to pay a fraction of the
cost it takes to mine, transport, and refine our metals.  The Lord and Lady
of the city ban these humans from further trade.

 250 K
  The first war against Bazabel. Using the remaining barbarian tribes as slaves
the army of humans attempt to storm the mountain.  The harsh conditions
and slopes make them easy targets for our crossbow men. They retreat.

400 K
 The first Ghoulish and Elven refugees arrive into our mountain.  News of a
great war against their kind by the humans reaches our ears as we take
these people under our wing.

425 K
  News of the destruction of the Ihra-Desh and Ayaniem empires reaches us.
The last survivors make their way to our mountain.  Preparations begin
to find them a new home.

500 K
 We find another great cavern, deep within the mountain. With our
dwarven kin, the city begins to take shape.

600 K
 After much delay and much work, the great city of Ihra-Ayan is built. The
ghoulish and elvish survivors of their once great homes relocate.  News of
another great army being marsheled first reaches us.

637 K
 The first half-barbarian peoples to make their way to us share their story
and their hatred of Bazabel and the Imperial forces. Talks begin on how
to deal with these new people in our lands.

641 K
  It is decided that any person that swears an oath to defy Bazabel shall
be granted sanctuary inside Kinterownt or Ihra-Ayan.

689 K
 Those calling themselves the Riders of the Claw begin their war against
Bazabel.  It is the first open rebellion that we have witnessed against
the city that has long since plagued us.

710 K
 The Riders of the Claw begin to accept the name they are given by
Bazabel, rebels. Comprised mostly of humans and half-spawn, their
numbers grow quickly and recover faster than ours. Their bases
are often found and destroyed. A council of gnome, dwarf, ghoul and
elves takes place to decide our position.

711 K
  The Rebels are granted full sanctuary and use of our cities. The Alliance
is formally signed against the growing threat of Bazabel. Ihra-Ayan becomes
the seat of the alliance and home to the Riders.

914 K
  The seige of the Fortress of Sorrow begins.  The dwarven kingdom
take heavy losses.  The Bazabel forces withdraw.

969 K
  The Fortress of Mt. Sorrow is taken.  The last of the dwarven forces
retreat back into their mine city.  Our forces mobilize to help defend
that city.

971 K
 Under General Zavish, the great mine city of the dwarfs is destroyed. We
lose almost half of our army to it's defense and the escape of the dwarves
into Kinterownt.  Zavish's head is taken by Lord Dilandou but only at the
sacrifice of Inthas and Mithras Ironshield.

996 K
 Warlord Zanzen begins a great seige of our city.  The experimental
Ethernaught and Battle-Ward are used.  With the support of Ihra-Ayan's
rangers attacking their flanks and our war-machines we push Zanzen
back after seven months of siege.

1006 K

  Warlord Zanzen and the Imperial forces move to the west. A new land
is discoverd by their mauraders.  They begin a long and as of now,
undecided war against a great city-state known as Alden.


1016 K
  Reports of travellers from the western land are confirmed. The Council has
met to determine the usefulness of these adventurers in our war.


~
